    - adr_0017  # 7495
    isbefore: []  # 7495
    duplicate_of: []  # 7495
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7495
    pr_ref:  # 7495
    description: "The Python analyzer emits ZERO `calls` edges for a call whose receiver is an attribute chain with\na non-module root. `Item.objects.create(...)` emits an edge; `o2.payments.create(...)` and\n`event.organizer.issued_gift_cards.create(...)` emit nothing at all.\n\nMEASURED, not inferred. Direct repro at\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/py_zero_edge_check.py, run against the real\n`analyze_python`, with a POSITIVE CONTROL in the same fixture so a harness fault is\ndistinguishable from an analyzer fault:\n\n  shape                                  source sites   edges emitted\n  os.getenv(...)      imported module          2              2   <- positive control\n  helper()            in-file function         2              2\n  obj.bar()           attr on a param          3              3\n  print(...)          builtin, bare Name       2              0   <- ZERO\n  obj.deep.method()   attribute chain          2              0   <- ZERO\n\nWHERE IT WAS FOUND. WI-vimon measured every `sink_after_source` failure on the cohort\n(caddy 15, pretix 61). caddy: 0 under-counts. pretix: 25 of 61 recorded FEWER sink call lines\nthan the source contains, and every one traces to this shape. Example, pretix\nsrc/tests/base/test_orders.py:\n\n    4083  ticket = Item.objects.create(...)                       -> edge emitted\n    4085  cp1 = CartPosition.objects.create(...)                  -> edge emitted\n    4088  gc1 = event.organizer.issued_gift_cards.create(...)     -> NO EDGE\n    4089  gc1.transactions.create(...)                            -> NO EDGE\n\nAll four are the same Django manager sink; the dst id is a single generic\n`python:django.db.models:0-0:create:external_symbol`.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE GUARD IT WAS FOUND UNDER. Within WI-vimon's scope the impact was\nsmall (exactly 1 of 76 pooled failures would have changed a verdict). But that population is\nbiased by construction: it only contains functions that ALREADY had at least one emitting sink\ncall, because a function with no sink edge never reaches guard2 at all.\n\n**The unmeasured population is the dangerous one: a function whose sink calls are ALL\nattribute-chain shaped has no sink edge, is never considered, and its flow is never reported.\nThat is a FALSE NEGATIVE — the expensive direction for a security tool — not a confidence\ndowngrade.** This is idiomatic Django (`obj.related.create()`, `obj.related.filter()`), so the\npopulation is plausibly large, but I did NOT size it and will not guess.\n\nWHAT TO MEASURE FIRST, before any fix:\n  1. Count functions in pretix containing at least one attribute-chain call to a catalogued\n     source/sink name and ZERO emitted edges to that callee. That is the false-negative\n     population. Use production's own catalog to decide \"catalogued\", not a hand-rolled list.\n  2. Separately count the `print()`-style bare-Name zero-edge shape — it is a different code\n     path and may have a different fix.\n  3. Only then size the fix, and check DIRECTION explicitly. More sink edges is expansive (more\n     sink sites considered) AND potentially suppressive (a flow that now passes guard2 can be\n     adjudicated, and adjudicated + a same-function sanitizer is the one route to `sanitized`,\n     taint.py:2569-2575). Net effect is NOT determined by WI-vimon's data.\n\nA SECOND, DISTINCT MECHANISM, filed here for the record because it shares this component and\nwas found by the same sweep, but measured at ZERO instances on the cohort: the same source-level\ncallee can SPLIT across dst ids by per-site receiver inference. `os.getenv` reached four ways\nyields `python:os:...:getenv` [7,8,9] and `python:external:...:getenv` [11]\n(meas/py_mixed_shape.py). Since `call_lines` is keyed on `(src, dst)`, each entry under-counts\nthat callee's true sites. Independently flagged by a Go-side reader as well. It would have shown\nas RECORDED_FEWER on caddy, which had none. Do not fold this into the fix above without\nre-measuring it.\n\nDO NOT re-derive the caddy/pretix numbers by hand — the instruments are persisted at\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/ and positive-control themselves."  # 7495
    fields:  # 7495
      statement: "Every call site of a catalogued taint source or sink in Python produces a calls edge, regardless of the receiver syntax used to reach the callee."  # 7495
      root_cause: "NOT YET LOCALIZED TO A LINE. Measured behaviour: analyze_python emits no calls edge when the callee is an attribute chain whose root is not an imported module (obj.deep.method(), o2.payments.create()), and none for a builtin bare Name (print()). Emission is correct for imported-module calls, in-file functions, and single-attribute calls on a parameter. The emitting code is _process_call in packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py; the exact branch that declines to emit was NOT read, only the input/output behaviour was measured."  # 7495
