  message: "Rolled up under class item INV-linub-nokij-gibim-rovok-moros-gural-domip-rimof (filed 2026-08-06), which now holds isbefore on this item. NOT a duplicate finding: the class exists because three per-analyzer items share one invariant, and because reading _match_propagation_entry / _lookup_named_entry showed the chain has FOUR links, not one. Emission (L2) is where these items sit; receiver evidence (L3) and the io-boundary F3 gate (L4) are downstream and can refuse an edge that emission successfully adds. So a fix scoped to emission alone can move zero findings while looking like a win at the analyzer. Do not start a fix here until the class measurement fills go/rust/objc and reads the declining branch in each failing analyzer."  # c54b
- op: discuss  # 2364
  at: '2026-08-06T11:31:01Z'  # 2364
  by: agent  # 2364
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2364
  clock: 3  # 2364
  nonce: '2364'  # 2364
  message: "THIS ITEM IS MANUFACTURING INV-busis BLOCKERS - a consequence neither thread recorded, measured 2026-08-06.\n\nINV-busis is held open because the section 3a walk loses track at sites it classifies as GENUINE NON-CALL escapes (field write / container subscript / closure), and that classification is what makes the 7a/7b scope ruling look load-bearing. Measured on hypergumbo self-analysis with the walk reporting its own escape sites (new escape_sites out-param on _ddg_taint_reaches, so nothing re-derives the logic): 24 of 66 resolved escape sites (36.4%) have a CFG node_type of literally `call`, and 99 of 150 escape sites (66.0%) have NO callee recorded at that line. Positive control fires - subprocess.run IS recorded at other sites, so the empties are real absences rather than a dead argument.\n\nThe sites name the mechanism directly: print(, isinstance(stderr, bytes), cmd.append(\"-q\"). Those are calls. This item measured exactly why they carry no edge - python emits ZERO call edges for attribute-chain receivers (cmd.append) and none for a builtin bare Name (print, isinstance). No call edge means no callees_at entry, which means _use_site_terminates cannot decide whether the callee consumes the value, which means escaped=True and the walk returns None.\n\nSO THE IMPACT OF THIS ITEM IS LARGER THAN ITS OWN FILING CLAIMS. The filing sizes it as a FALSE NEGATIVE (a function whose sink calls are all attribute-chain has no sink edge and is never reported) and says the population is unmeasured. That is still true and still the headline. But it ALSO degrades every walk that passes through such a call - the flow is not missed, it is downgraded from a decidable verdict to unknown, which is what holds INV-busis open.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS FOR SEQUENCING: fixing this item is a false-negative fix in the SAFE direction and needs no owner ruling, yet it removes blockers from INV-busis that were being attributed to an ADR-0017 7a/7b scope exclusion. Work it before anything scoped as field-sensitivity.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING for whoever picks it up: emitting these call edges gives callees_at entries, which lets _use_site_terminates start returning True at those sites, which produces MORE False verdicts from the walk. Since PR #214 a False earns sanitized and a sanitized flow is dropped. So this fix can SUPPRESS. Measure on findings, both signs. The WI-joluk coverage gate (merged 2026-08-06) is the guard that makes that safe to attempt.\n\nCAVEATS: python only, self-analysis, not a neutral corpus. The three Go repos available yielded 15 resolved sites between them - too few to share. Instruments: meas/escape_shapes.py, escape_hypergumbo.log."  # 2364
- op: discuss  # 98e3
  at: '2026-08-06T13:05:12Z'  # 98e3
  by: agent  # 98e3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 98e3
  clock: 4  # 98e3
  nonce: '98e3'  # 98e3
  message: "FIX FOR THE ATTRIBUTE-CHAIN HALF, with the direction measured. Premise re-verified on dev 81a62fcf97 with a positive control before any code changed: os.getenv (imported module) 1 edge, helper() in-file 1 edge, obj.bar() attr-on-param 1 edge, print(...) builtin bare Name ZERO, obj.deep.method() attribute chain ZERO. Reproduces this item exactly.\n\nROOT CAUSE NOW LOCALIZED TO A LINE, which this item said it was not. py.py, the catch-all `elif isinstance(func, ast.Attribute)` branch: _unwind_attribute_chain returns a chain for event.organizer.issued_gift_cards.create (root `event` IS an ast.Name), but the emit is gated on `if root_name in module_imports and len(chain_attrs) >= 2`. A chain rooted at a LOCAL fails the first conjunct and falls through with no else, so nothing is emitted. The single-attribute form obj.bar() has emitted an external-module edge since WI-fuvuj for exactly this reason. Depth was the only difference and nothing justified it. FIX: an else that emits python:external:0-0:<method>:unresolved with call_construct=method, placed inside the module-import branch so the class-rooted Django marker (which emits a module-qualified django.db.models edge earlier) keeps winning - pinned by its own test.\n\nI ALSO CORRECTED TWO OF MY OWN CLAIMS BEFORE THEY TRAVELLED.\n(1) I asserted this item suppresses builtins.open sink detection. FALSE. open() DOES emit (python:builtins:0-0:open:unresolved) and matches the catalogued builtins.open host_fs sink - py.py has an EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES whitelist for it. Measured: open YES; print/len/isinstance/eval/exec/input/sorted NO. So the builtin gap is a small whitelist, not builtins in general.\n(2) The two shapes this item names have OPPOSITE directions and must not be fixed as one. ATTRIBUTE CHAIN can miss a catalogued sink (Django obj.related.create) = recall up. BUILTIN BARE NAME mostly turns a call into an escape site; fixing it only helps where a TERMINATING summary exists (print has one, len/isinstance do not), and where it helps it produces MORE False, which since #214 earns sanitized and DROPS a flow = suppressive. Only the attribute-chain half is fixed here. The builtin half is deliberately NOT fixed and should be measured separately.\n\nDIRECTION MEASURED, both signs, on kserve: evidence_rows 22 -> 22, sanitized 0 -> 0, violated verdicts 4 -> 4, methods identical, escape_sites 3 -> 3. ZERO CHANGE. Analyzer level, cache-free: the fix adds 2,155 call edges on kserve/python. So capability moved and adjudication did not - the WI-nonad shape. No suppression introduced, which is the half that mattered.\n\nSTALE-READ CHECK, because byte-identical before/after is the L11 tell: the cache key includes an analyzer-identity hash over every installed .py, and it genuinely differs between the arms (dfb37ba5a9bfc9f9 with the fix, 9fff4c1df3d299e5 without), so both arms analysed fresh. The zero is real.\n\nWHY ZERO HERE AND STILL WORTH LANDING: the 2,155 new edges are logger.info, dict.get, str.replace, argparse.add_argument - none catalogued sinks. The population that WOULD move is Django-shaped (obj.related.create), and pretix, where this item four-adjacent-lines measurement came from, is NOT on this box. So: no measured recall gain on available repos, no suppression, and the false-negative route closed before a repo that exercises it arrives. Same reasoning as WI-joluk.\n\nSTILL UNMEASURED, as the filing says: the size of the population whose sink calls are ALL chain-shaped. This fix makes that population measurable for the first time; it does not size it."  # 98e3
